  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "ir-ci1",
      "severity": "major",
      "disposition": "fixed",
      "reason": "Git 2.56.1 terminal wording was not recognized by the newly added diagnostic tests. Centralize exactly the observed bad and quoted-bad terminal forms. Count all recognized terminal records before validating a single 40-hex SHA; use the same matcher for absence assertions, including missing-SHA prefixes. Require an anchored complete ambiguity heading in either observed form. Keep original target SHA, skip, abort, exit-code and candidate-set assertions. Add five deterministic format regression methods. 10/10 local methods passed with no skips. Independent replay accepted both actual remote terminal records and the real ambiguity output, and rejected exit127 with a terminal, a valid plus malformed duplicate terminal, and an actual quoted terminal in the absence path. Existing real Git histories still execute the published wrapper and compare exact targets. not-yet-completed for the updated PR head; required before merge, independently of this source finding closure."
    }
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No local Git2.56.1 binary was executed; local test environment is Git2.52.0. The quoted variant was verified by actual CI-text replay and deterministic regressions, pending fresh hosted execution.",
